Splunk Index Creation Methods
Follow the steps to create an index using the Splunk Web interface.

Navigate to https://<your-splunk-host>:8000. Log in with an admin-level account.

From the top menu, select Settings, within the Data category, select Indexes.

Select New Index.

Configure the Index Settings:

Index Name: Enter a unique name (e.g., navsec_security_events).

App Context: Choose an app if applicable (default is search).

Home Path: Leave as default (unless a specific storage location is required).

Cold Path: Optional, for moving older data to secondary storage.

Thawed Path: Optional, used for restoring archived data.

Max Size (MB): Set storage limits if required.

Data Retention: Set retention period (e.g., 30 days, 1 year).

Enable Data Integrity Check: Optional, for compliance-focused deployments.

Select Save.

Follow the steps to create an index using configuration files.

Navigate to the indexes Configuration File, using the following commands


bash

$SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/<your-app>/local/indexes.conf
Open indexes.conf. NOTE: If it does not exist, create a new file named indexes.conf.

Add the index definition, using the commands below:


ini

[navsec_security_events] homePath = $SPLUNK_DB/navsec_security_events/db coldPath = $SPLUNK_DB/navsec_security_events/colddb thawedPath = $SPLUNK_DB/navsec_security_events/thaweddb maxTotalDataSizeMB = 50000 frozenTimePeriodInSecs = 31536000  # 1 year
Save the configuration.

Restart Splunk to apply changes:


bash

./splunk restart
